  "articleBody": "When it comes to finish carpentry, a great installation means lasting beauty. But it's easy to stumble if you're not careful. One of the biggest pitfalls is not verifying who will actually be doing the installation work. You want experienced hands, not a new trainee learning on your home. Another common mistake is skipping thorough checks on door reveal consistency; uneven gaps around doors are a dead giveaway of a rushed or poor job. It's also a big no-no to order materials, especially custom items, before fully understanding your opening conditions or any special sizing needs. You might end up with pieces that just don't fit! Protecting the work area and cleaning up daily are often overlooked, leading to damage or a messy site. And always, always ask about the installer's experience with similar projects, their billing method, and if they offer a detailed contract with a workmanship warranty. These things protect your investment. When you’re dealing with things like custom openings, matching existing finishes, or if square and level are critical, a qualified professional really shines. They’ll catch these issues before they become major headaches, ensuring a beautiful, durable finish. Don't take chances with your home's finish work—contact HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to ensure a professional installation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
